# Agent worktrees are scratch checkouts, never part of a commit.
.claude/worktrees/

# Environment files. .env was tracked in this repository, which is fine
# for the publishable/anon key it held — that key is meant to be public
# and is protected by row-level security — but it is exactly the wrong
# place for a service role key, an AI backend key or a Stripe key, all of
# which the app reads from the environment. Ignored so a secret pasted
# into .env can never be committed by accident. Names and shapes are
# documented in .env.example, which is tracked and holds no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
